@startuml client-platform-entities
' SPEC: _spec/packages/client-platform/entities.puml
' purpose: @chess-coach/client-platform — the one client-device table both apps
' ask, and the rule that keeps keyboard copy honest. Authority: shipped.
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title client-platform · one device table, two consumers

package "packages/client-platform (framework-free)" {
  component "resolveClientOS(ua, hintPlatform, maxTouchPoints)\n→ linux | macos | windows | ios | android | unknown" as OS <<app>>
  component "detectClientDevice()\n→ { os, isMobile }  · reads navigator once" as DEV <<app>>
  component "isDesktopClient({ device, finePointer })\n→ boolean  · pure predicate" as PRED <<app>>
  component "DESKTOP_POINTER_MQ\n""(pointer: fine) and (hover: hover)""" as MQ <<db>>
}

package "consumers" {
  component "apps/ui services/platform.ts\ndetectPlatform() → PlatformInfo\n(Tailscale label · download · docs)" as UI <<app>>
  component "apps/starchess hooks/useIsDesktopClient.ts\nuseMediaQuery(DESKTOP_POINTER_MQ) + device" as SC <<app>>
  component "GasRack cancel hint\nEsc copy vs drop-outside copy" as GAS <<async>>
}

DEV ARROW_MAIN OS : ua + UA-CH hint + touch points
UI ARROW_MAIN DEV : os · isMobile only
SC ARROW_MAIN DEV
SC ARROW_MAIN MQ : live band
SC ARROW_MAIN PRED
GAS ARROW_QUEUE SC : which half of the contract to name

note right of PRED
  **Both opinions must agree.** Either signal alone ships wrong copy:
  * fine pointer alone → offers **Esc** to a phone with a Bluetooth mouse;
  * desktop UA alone → offers **Esc** to a Windows tablet held in two hands.
  Disagreement ⇒ say nothing about keys. The drop-outside sentence is true
  on every device, so it is the safe default, never a downgrade.

  ""isDesktopClient"" takes ""finePointer"" as an **argument** rather than
  reading ""matchMedia"" itself: that keeps the package framework-free and the
  rule unit-testable without a DOM.
end note

note bottom of OS
  iPadOS 13+ ships a **desktop Safari UA** — ""maxTouchPoints > 1"" is the only
  tell, so it is passed in rather than sniffed. Safari implements no UA-CH at
  all, so the UA string stays the fallback, never dead code.
  Pinned by ""apps/starchess/src/__tests__/platform/clientPlatform.test.ts""
  (the suite lives in the consumer: this package ships no runner, same as
  ""engine-core"").
end note

note bottom of UI
  ""PlatformInfo"" keeps the **Tailscale** mapping (label / download / install
  docs) — app business, deliberately not in the shared package. The UA table it
  used to own moved here; ""OS"" and ""ClientOS"" are the same union.
end note
@enduml
